    <p class="micro">Legal</p>
    <h1 class="doc-h">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="updated">Last updated: August 2026</p>

    <div class="prose">
      <p><b>The short version:</b> we store the minimum needed to sign you in,
      your picks and settings stay on your device, everything else is anonymous,
      we don't sell your data, and you can ask us to delete your profile any
      time.</p>

      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><b>Your profile</b>: when you sign in with Google we store your name,
        email address, and profile photo URL. We use Google Sign-In; we never
        see your password.</li>
        <li><b>Anonymous analytics</b>: which screens you open, which buttons
        you use, which settings you toggle, and whether alerts and celebrations
        reached your screen - plus crash reports (via Firebase
        Analytics/Crashlytics) so we can keep the app working. This is
        anonymized - it's tied to a random app-instance identifier, never to
        your name or sign-in.</li>
        <li><b>Celebration taps</b>: when you tap the ball after a goal, your
        taps are counted toward a worldwide total for that match. These are
        anonymized and only ever stored as aggregate numbers - never tied to
        you.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>What we don't collect</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Any personal information beyond what is listed above.</li>
        <li>The teams you follow and your app settings (theme, which events you
        want to see) stay on your device - we never send them to our server.
        Following a team or changing a setting is counted in the anonymous
        usage statistics above, but that is an aggregate number, not an
        account: your list of teams and your settings live only on your Mac,
        and there is nothing on our side to restore them from.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Where it lives</h2>
      <p>Your profile is stored on Google Cloud (Firestore) in the United
      States. Anonymous analytics are processed by Firebase.</p>

      <h2>Deleting your data</h2>
      <p>Email
      <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">{{ site.email }}</a>
      and we'll delete your profile for you.</p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p><a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">{{ site.email }}</a></p>
    </div>
